%N A400462 Numbers k such that the trajectory of k->ord(-2,k) reaches 1 before reaching a number not coprime to -2. Here ord(b,k) is the multiplicative order of b modulo k.
%C A400462 Closed under multiplication.
%C A400462 Also numbers k such that the trajectory of k->ord(-8,k) reaches 1 before reaching a number not coprime to -8. See A400096 for general discussions.
%H A400462 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400462/b400462.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..3666</a> (all terms <= 10^10)
%e A400462 Powers of 3 are terms: 3^n -> 3^(n-1) -> ... -> 3 -> 1;
%e A400462 571 is a term: 571 -> 57 -> 9 -> 3 -> 1;
%e A400462 1459 is a term: 1459 -> 243 -> 81 -> 27 -> 9 -> 3 -> 1;
%e A400462 160465489 is a term: 160465489 -> 57 -> 9 -> 3 -> 1.
%t A400462 (* okQ is defined at A400096 *)
%t A400462 Select[Range[30000], okQ[#, -2] &] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 26 2026 *)
%o A400462 (PARI) isok(n, -2) \\ see A400096 for isok
%Y A400462 See A400096 for list of sequences in other bases.
%K A400462 nonn,new
%O A400462 1,2
